WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:04.701
♪♪

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:07.400
Narrator:
BOOK MAKING HAS EVOLVED
OVER TIME.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.334
FROM SCROLLS TO WRITING ON
SHEETS OF PAPER BOUND TOGETHER

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.434
TO THE INVENTION
OF THE PRINTING PRESS,

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:17.200
PEOPLE CONTINUE TO DEVELOP
NEW WAYS OF RECORDING HISTORY.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.801
TODAY, THANKS
TO DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY,

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:23.767
THE POSSIBILITIES OF RECORDING
THE SPOKEN WORD ARE ENDLESS.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.400
[ SUSPENSEFUL HIP HOP PLAYS ]

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.334
A FINE BOOK MAKING SPECIALIST

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:30.934
MAKES JUST A FEW LIMITED
EDITION BOOKS PER YEAR,

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:34.000
USING TRADITIONAL PRINTING
AND BINDING TECHNIQUES.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.467
♪♪

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:41.067
PRODUCTION BEGINS WITH A CASE
OF TINY BRASS MOLDS.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.300
ONE MOLD, CALLED A MATRIX,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.567
CONTAINS LETTERS, NUMBERS,
AND PUNCTUATION MARKS.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.901
♪♪

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:52.734
A TYPECASTING SPECIALIST
INSERTS THE MATRIX CASE

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.934
INTO A MACHINE CALLED
A MONOTYPE COMPOSITION CASTER...

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.734
♪♪

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:02.100
AND MELTS LEAD ALLOY INGOTS
IN THE MACHINE'S GAS-HEATED POT.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.634
♪♪

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.634
GUIDED BY A COMPUTER,
THE MACHINE CASTS

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:12.634
ONE CHARACTER AT A TIME
FOR EVERY WORD OF THE BOOK.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:17.334
THE COMPUTER PROGRAM ASSIGNS
A LOCATION CODE TO EVERY MATRIX.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:20.167
TO CAST A CHARACTER,
THE PROGRAM COMMUNICATES

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:23.067
A SPECIFIC CODE
THROUGH PLASTIC TUBES

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.067
WHILE PUFFS OF AIR ALIGN
THAT CHARACTER'S MATRIX

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.734
WITH THE INJECTION NOZZLE.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:31.167
THE NOZZLE DISPENSES
MOLTEN LEAD INTO THE MATRIX,

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.434
WHILE THE MACHINE EJECTS
THE CAST CHARACTER

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:36.033
ONTO A TRAY CALLED THE GALLEY.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.033
AS THE LINES OF TEXT
EXIT THE MACHINE,

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:42.133
THE TYPECAST SPECIALIST
INSERTS A STRIP OF LEAD

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:46.767
TO CREATE SPACING, CALLED
LEADING, BETWEEN EACH LINE.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.634
HE TRANSFERS THE GALLEY
TO THE PRESS ROOM,

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:52.968
WHERE A PROOFING PRESS
SPREADS INK ON THE TYPE.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:56.300
HE PLACES A SHEET OF NEWSPRINT
OVER THE GALLEY

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.634
AND RELEASES
AN IMPRESSION ROLLER.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:01.167
THE ROLLER PRINTS THE
CHARACTERS ONTO THE PAPER,

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:02.634
GENERATING A PROOF.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:07.834
♪♪

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.033
MEANWHILE,
A TYPESETTER ASSEMBLES

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:12.133
THE LARGER DISPLAY COPY MANUALLY

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:16.033
BY PLACING INDIVIDUAL LETTERS
INTO A COMPOSITION STICK.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:19.834
THIS METHOD WAS USED FOR ALL
COPY PRIOR TO THE INVENTION

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:23.701
OF AUTOMATIC TYPECASTING
MACHINES IN THE 1890s.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.601
♪♪

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.901
BOOKS PRINTED
IN LARGE SIZES OF TYPE

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.901
MUST BE MADE ENTIRELY
BY MANUAL TYPESET.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.734
♪♪

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.067
ONCE COMPLETE,

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.300
MULTIPLE GALLEYS THAT MAKE UP
SEVERAL PAGES OF THE BOOK

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.267
ARE PLACED IN A STEEL FRAME
CALLED A CHASE

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.634
AND LOADED
INTO THE PRINTING PRESS.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.601
♪♪

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:49.200
THIS CYLINDER PRESS FEEDS
ONE SHEET OF PAPER AT A TIME

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.634
TO GRIPPERS THAT PULL THE PAPER
AROUND A CYLINDRICAL ROLLER.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.434
AS THE ROLLER ROTATES,

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.968
THE PAPER DROPS
ONTO THE INKED TYPE,

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:01.167
PRINTING THE CHARACTERS
INTO THE SHEET.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:05.434
ONE PRESS SHEET TYPICALLY
CONTAINS EIGHT PAGES PER SIDE.

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:07.801
ANOTHER MACHINE
FOLDS THE SHEETS.

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:10.234
THEN, BOOKBINDERS
MANUALLY COLLATE

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.567
GROUPS OF 16 CONSECUTIVE PAGES

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:15.834
TO FORM SECTIONS OF THE BOOK,
CALLED SIGNATURES.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.400
♪♪

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.801
NEXT, A BOOKBINDER SEWS
THE SIGNATURES TOGETHER,

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:25.901
ONE AT A TIME, UNTIL THE BOOK
IS FULLY ASSEMBLED.

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:29.200
THIS METHOD OF BOOKBINDING,
CALLED SMYTH SEWN BINDING,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.434
AFTER ITS 19th CENTURY INVENTOR,
IS OF THE HIGHEST QUALITY

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:37.100
BECAUSE PAGES CAN'T FALL OUT
OR BE REMOVED.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.801
♪♪

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:46.701
LIKE THE BINDING, THE BOOK COVER
IS METICULOUSLY HANDCRAFTED.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.200
A BOOKBINDER HOT GLUES
A PIECE OF CLOTH

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.667
TO THE BACK OF THE COVER.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:55.167
THE COVER IS MADE OF FLEXIBLE
PAPER AND THICK CARDBOARD.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.400
♪♪

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.567
THEN, SHE FLATTENS
THE CLOTH ON ALL SIDES.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.601
♪♪

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.467
USING A RAZOR BLADE,

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:09.033
THE BOOKBINDER MAKES
A SLIT FOR THE CLOTH,

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:11.868
WHERE SHE'LL PLACE
A RECESSED LABEL LATER.

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.334
THIS ENABLES THE CLOTH
TO SPREAD OUT

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:17.100
AND FORM TO THE SPINE'S
ROUNDED SHAPE.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.067
THE CLOTH IS PRESSED FIRMLY

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.067
AGAINST THE
STRUCTURAL COMPONENTS

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.234
WITH A PLASTIC TOOL
CALLED A BONE.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:24.601
♪♪

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.834
ANOTHER BOOKBINDER
ATTACHES THE COVER

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:30.100
TO THE BOUND PAGES,
CALLED THE BOOK BLOCK.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.501
FIRST, SHE APPLIES GLUE
TO BOTH COMPONENTS.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:35.434
♪♪

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:38.767
THEN, SHE POSITIONS
THE BOOK BLOCK ON THE COVER...

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.667
♪♪

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.501
...AND PRESSES THEM TOGETHER.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:47.000
♪♪

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.968
SHE PLACES THE BOOK
IN A NIPPING PRESS

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.033
THAT PUTS PRESSURE
AROUND THE SPINE,

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:55.000
FUSING THE BOOK BLOCK
AND COVER TOGETHER.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.767
THEN, THE FRONT
AND BACK OF THE COVER

00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:59.834
ARE GLUED TO THE FIRST
AND LAST PAGES OF THE BOOK.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.534
♪♪

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.501
THE BOOK THEN SITS
IN ANOTHER PRESS OVERNIGHT,

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.701
BRINGING THIS BOOKMAKING
STORY TO A CLOSE.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:10.601
♪♪

